  "instance_name": "buchenwald_concentration_camp",
  "label": "Buchenwald Concentration Camp",
  "description": "A Nazi concentration camp located in Weimarer Land, Germany, established in 1937. It was one of the largest and most notorious camps, where hundreds of thousands of prisoners, including Jews, Poles, Soviet prisoners of war, Roma, and others, were murdered. The crematorium at Buchenwald was used for mass murder, not for the cremation of anti-Nazi German women. The camp was liberated by American forces in April 1945.",
